# Rust Modularity

Do not grow Rust crates as a monolithic `lib.rs`.

When editing any Rust crate in this repo:

- Keep `src/lib.rs` as a thin module/export entry point.
- Put real logic in focused modules, for example `ffi.rs`, `text.rs`, `paths.rs`, `cue.rs`, `mpc.rs`, `m3u.rs`, `pls.rs`, or similarly scoped files.
- Put C ABI boundary code in `ffi.rs` or a clearly named FFI module.
- Put parser/algorithm logic in format-specific or domain-specific modules.
- Add tests close to the module they validate.
- Before adding new functionality to an existing Rust crate, split the crate first if `lib.rs` contains substantial implementation logic.

Bad:

```rust
// lib.rs
// hundreds of lines of FFI, parsing, memory management, and tests together
```

Good:

```rust
// lib.rs
mod ffi;
mod parser;
mod text;
```
